       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't resolve either concern.\n\n- **You're not the prescriber.** The confirmation needs to come from the clinician responsible for this patient, not from the finance office.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg/day is about double the maximum recommended metformin dose of 2,550 mg/day. A 1,700 mg single dose is also well above the usual 1,000 mg per-dose limit. Nothing you've told me about the patient (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would make this dose appropriate.\n\nI also made a typo in my last message. It should have said a single dose is typically no more than 1,000 mg.\n\nThe prescribing clinician can review the dose and enter the order directly. They can also ask me to enter a corrected order, such as 850 mg three times daily, and I'll do that. I'm also happy to help with anything on the finance side."
